  ('minister', 'minister', '''ministә', E'n. 部长, 牧师, 公使\nvi. 服侍, 救助, 主持宗教仪式', E'n. a person appointed to a high office in the government\nn. a diplomat representing one government to another; ranks below ambassador\nn. the job of a head of a government department\nv. attend to the wants and needs of others', '', 5, true, '{gk,cet4,cet6,ky,ielts}', 294, 1910, 's:ministers/i:ministering/p:ministered/3:ministers/d:ministered'),
