  ('interview', 'interview', '''intәvju:', E'n. 面谈, 访问, 接见, 面试\nvt. 接见, 对...进行面谈(试)', E'n. the questioning of a person (or a conversation in which information is elicited); often conducted by journalists\nv. conduct an interview in television, newspaper, and radio reporting\nv. discuss formally with (somebody) for the purpose of an evaluation\nv. go for an interview in the hope of being hired', '', 4, true, '{zk,gk,cet4,cet6,ky,ielts}', 1421, 944, 's:interviews/d:interviewed/p:interviewed/i:interviewing/3:interviews'),
