  ('realise', 'realise', '''riәlaiz,''ri:-', 'vt. 实现, 认识到, 体会到, 了解, 认清, 使显得逼真, 变卖财产为现钱', E'v earn on some commercial or business transaction; earn as salary or wages\nv convert into cash; of goods and property\nv expand or complete (a part in a piece of baroque music) by supplying the harmonies indicated in the figured bass\nv make real or concrete; give reality or substance to\nv be fully aware or cognizant of\nv perceive (an idea or situation) mentally', '', 0, false, '{zk,gk,ky}', 1018, null, 'p:realised/d:realised/i:realising/3:realises'),
  ('context', 'context', '''kɒntekst', E'n. 上下文, 背景, 来龙去脉\nn. 上下文\n[计] 上下文', E'n. discourse that surrounds a language unit and helps to determine its interpretation\nn. the set of facts or circumstances that surround a situation or event', '', 3, true, '{cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 1019, 1427, 's:contexts'),
