  ('gas', 'gas', 'gæs', E'n. 气体, 汽油, 瓦斯\n[化] 气体; 煤气; 瓦斯; 毒气', E'n. the state of matter distinguished from the solid and liquid states by: relatively low density and viscosity; relatively great expansion and contraction with changes in pressure and temperature; the ability to diffuse readily; and the spontaneous tendency to become distributed uniformly throughout any container\nn. a fluid in the gaseous state having neither independent shape nor volume and being able to expand indefinitely\nv. attack with gas; subject to gas fumes', '', 4, true, '{gk,cet4,ky}', 1205, 1023, 's:gases/i:gassing/p:gassed/3:gasses/d:gassed'),
