  ('proportion', 'proportion', 'prә''pɒ:ʃәn', E'n. 比例, 比率, 均衡, 部分, 面积\nvt. 使成比例, 使均衡', E'n. the quotient obtained when the magnitude of a part is divided by the magnitude of the whole\nn. magnitude or extent\nn. the relation between things (or parts of things) with respect to their comparative quantity, magnitude, or degree\nn. harmonious arrangement or relation of parts or elements within a whole (as in a design)', '', 3, true, '{cet4,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts}', 1247, 3063, 's:proportions/d:proportioned/i:proportioning/p:proportioned/3:proportions'),
