  ('universal', 'universal', '.ju:ni''vә:sl', E'a. 全世界的, 普遍的, 宇宙的, 通用的\nn. 一般概念', E'n. (linguistics) a grammatical rule (or other linguistic feature) that is found in all languages\nn. (logic) a proposition that asserts something of all members of a class\nn. a behavioral convention or pattern characteristic of all members of a particular culture or of all human beings\ns. applicable to or common to all members of a group or set', '', 2, false, '{gk,cet4,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts}', 2968, 2642, 's:universals'),
  ('spin', 'spin', 'spin', E'n. 旋转, 自旋, 疾驰, 情绪低落\nvt. 纺织, 纺, 使旋转, 编造\nvi. 纺纱, 吐丝, 作茧, 结网, 旋转, 自旋, 疾驰', E'n. a swift whirling motion (usually of a missile)\nn. the act of rotating rapidly\nn. a short drive in a car\nn. a distinctive interpretation (especially as used by politicians to sway public opinion)', '', 3, true, '{gk,cet4,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 3841, 2644, 'i:spinning/p:spun/d:spun/3:spins/s:spins'),
