  ('satisfaction', 'satisfaction', '.sætis''fækʃәn', E'n. 满足, 满意, 快事, 赔偿, 赎罪, 报仇的机会\n[经] 偿还, 赎回', E'n. the contentment one feels when one has fulfilled a desire, need, or expectation\nn. (law) the payment of a debt or fulfillment of an obligation\nn. act of fulfilling a desire or need or appetite', '', 2, true, '{gk,cet4,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts}', 2683, 2779, 's:satisfactions'),
  ('remote', 'remote', 'ri''mәut', E'a. 遥远的, 偏僻的, 疏远的, 微少的\n[计] 远程, 远程访问实用程序', E'n a device that can be used to control a machine or apparatus from a distance\ns located far away spatially\ns very unlikely\ns separate or apart in time\ns inaccessible and sparsely populated;\na far apart in relevance or relationship or kinship', '', 3, true, '{gk,cet4,cet6,ky,toefl}', 2684, 2778, 'r:remoter/t:remotest'),
  ('resort', 'resort', 'ri''zɒ:t', E'n. 度假胜地, 手段, 凭借, 常去之地\nvi. 诉诸, 常去', 'n. a hotel located in a resort area', '', 3, true, '{cet4,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 3200, 2684, 's:resorts/i:resorting/d:resorted/p:resorted/3:resorts'),
