  ('bubble', 'bubble', '''bʌbl', E'n. 泡沫\nvi. 冒泡, 沸腾\nvt. 使冒泡, 滔滔不绝地说', E'n. a hollow globule of gas (e.g., air or carbon dioxide)\nn. an impracticable and illusory idea\nn. a dome-shaped covering made of transparent glass or plastic\nv. form, produce, or emit bubbles', '', 2, true, '{cet4,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 5570, 4104, 's:bubbles/i:bubbling/p:bubbled/d:bubbled/3:bubbles'),
