  ('contempt', 'contempt', 'kәn''tempt', E'n. 轻视, 轻蔑\n[法] 藐视, 侮辱, 轻视', E'n. lack of respect accompanied by a feeling of intense dislike\nn. a manner that is generally disrespectful and contemptuous\nn. open disrespect for a person or thing\nn. a willful disobedience to or disrespect for the authority of a court or legislative body', '', 2, false, '{cet4,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 4753, 6277, 's:contempts'),
