  ('coherent', 'coherent', 'kәu''hiәrәnt', 'a. 互相耦合的, 清晰的, 明了的，凝聚性的, 连贯的', E'a. marked by an orderly, logical, and aesthetically consistent relation of parts\ns. capable of thinking and expressing yourself in a clear and consistent manner\na. (physics) of waves having a constant phase relation\ns. sticking together', '', 1, false, '{cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 5289, 7004, ''),
  ('erupt', 'erupt', 'i''rʌpt', E'vi. 爆发\nvt. 喷出', E'v. start abruptly\nv. erupt or intensify suddenly\nv. start to burn or burst into flames\nv. break out', '', 2, false, '{gk,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 6441, 5291, 'p:erupted/d:erupted/3:erupts/i:erupting'),
  ('terminate', 'terminate', '''tә:mineit', E'a. 有结尾的, (可)结束的\nvi. 结束, 终止, 满期\nvt. 使停止, 使结束, 使终止\n[计] 终止', E'v bring to an end or halt\nv have an end, in a temporal, spatial, or quantitative sense; either spatial or metaphorical\nv be the end of; be the last or concluding part of\nv terminate the employment of; discharge from an office or position', '', 2, false, '{cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 5291, 7189, 'd:terminated/i:terminating/3:terminates/p:terminated'),
