  ('rebellion', 'rebellion', 'ri''beljәn', E'n. 谋反, 叛乱, 反抗\n[法] 造反, 反叛, 叛乱', E'n. refusal to accept some authority or code or convention\nn. organized opposition to authority; a conflict in which one faction tries to wrest control from another', '', 2, false, '{cet4,cet6,ky,toefl}', 5367, 6331, 's:rebellions'),
