  ('transplant', 'transplant', 'træns''plɑ:nt', E'vt. 使移居, 移植, 使迁移\nvi. 移居, 耐移植\nn. 移居者, 移植', E'n. an operation moving an organ from one organism (the donor) to another (the recipient)\nn. the act of removing something from one location and introducing it in another location\nv. lift and reset in another soil or situation\nv. be transplantable', '', 2, false, '{cet4,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts}', 8061, 5386, 's:transplants/d:transplanted/p:transplanted/i:transplanting/3:transplants'),
  ('explosive', 'explosive', 'ik''splәusiv', E'n. 炸药, 爆破音\na. 易爆发的, 爆炸的, 暴躁的', E'n. a chemical substance that undergoes a rapid chemical change (with the production of gas) on being heated or struck\na. serving to explode or characterized by explosion or sudden outburst\ns. liable to lead to sudden change or violence\ns. sudden and loud', '', 2, false, '{cet4,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 6878, 5387, 's:explosives'),
  ('illuminate', 'illuminate', 'i''lju:mineit', E'vt. 照明, 用灯装饰, 阐明, 说明, 使灿烂\nvi. 照亮, 用灯装饰', 'v. add embellishments and paintings to (medieval manuscripts)', '', 1, false, '{cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 6519, 5388, 'd:illuminated/3:illuminates/i:illuminating/p:illuminated'),
