  ('flaw', 'flaw', 'flɒ:', E'n. 缺点, 裂纹, 瑕疵, 一阵狂风\n[化] 划痕; 裂缝; 裂纹', E'n. defect or weakness in a person''s character\nn. an imperfection in a plan or theory or legal document that causes it to fail or that reduces its effectiveness\nv. add a flaw or blemish to; make imperfect or defective', '', 1, false, '{cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 8453, 5399, 's:flaws/i:flawing/p:flawed/3:flaws/d:flawed'),
