  ('gauge', 'gauge', 'geidʒ', E'n. 标准度量, 计量器\nvt. 精确计量, 估计\n[计] 线规', E'n. a measuring instrument for measuring and indicating a quantity such as the thickness of wire or the amount of rain etc.\nn. accepted or approved instance or example of a quantity or quality against which others are judged or measured or compared\nn. the distance between the rails of a railway or between the wheels of a train\nn. the thickness of wire', '', 2, false, '{cet4,cet6,ky,toefl,ielts,gre}', 6448, 6046, 's:gauges/d:gauged/i:gauging/p:gauged/3:gauges'),
